	(text "White LED channel: Legend-Si LGS63032EP boost, 16 x OSRAM DURIS E 2835 3000K CRI90 as 2 parallel strings of 8.\nString A (LED1-8) = inner ring, string B (LED9-16) = outer ring.\nI_total = V_FB / (R3 || R5) = 0.2 V / 1.54R = 130 mA -> ~65 mA per string (LED max 90 mA).\nR3 || R5 = 2.2R || 5.1R, both JLCPCB Basic. Up to ~180 mA total is within the 1.5 A min switch limit.\n8-LED strings have ~30R dynamic resistance, so 0.2 V Vf mismatch -> ~7 mA imbalance.\nV_string ~ 8 x 2.9 V = 23.2 V. OVP (R6/R7) trips at 31.3 V if both strings open -\nbelow D2 (40 V) and C2 (50 V) ratings. OVP does NOT catch a single open string (the other\nstring then carries the full current): power up new boards current-limited.\n~3 W LED power, ~0.76 A from 5 V. Peak switch current ~0.9 A (1.5 A min limit). Dmax >= 85 %.\nDimming: PWM on EN, 100 Hz - 100 kHz, converted to constant current (flicker-free).\nR8 100k keeps EN low (LEDs off) while the ESP32 boots. Pin 6 is NC - leave floating.\nC1 is the U2 input cap and main 5 V bulk cap - place next to U2. Exposed pad (pin 9) to GND with vias.\nRT1 sits among the white LEDs for thermal derating (Vout = 3V3 * RT1/(R4+RT1)), B = 3950 K.\nFB layout: run the FB trace from the R3/R5 top pads straight to U2 pin 1 (FB), away from\nSW/L1/D2. Return the R3/R5 GND pads to the plane next to U2 GND, not through the C1/C2\nswitching-current return path. No Kelvin connection needed at 1.54R / 200 mV."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
